IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il37-nouns`
IMPORT `il37-committee`

-- Tests for the quorum, the vintages and the transitional window, s 4A, s 4B and s 7(4). Row IL-37.
-- Every day below is a HYPOTHETICAL fixture chosen so that the expected value can be counted by hand; none is a date the Law or the Knesset has fixed.
-- Expected values are worked from the text of the instrument (SH 3388 pp. 434-436), never from the code's output.

§ `Fixtures`

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN, b IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A BOOLEAN, d IS A BOOLEAN, e IS A BOOLEAN, f IS A BOOLEAN, g IS A BOOLEAN, h IS A BOOLEAN, i IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `A member serving on the committee`
`the nine from the 26th Knesset in order` MEANS
    LIST (`A member serving on the committee` OF `the President of the Supreme Court`, a),
         (`A member serving on the committee` OF `another justice of the Supreme Court whom the body of its justices chose`, b),
         (`A member serving on the committee` OF `another justice of the Supreme Court whom the body of its justices chose`, c),
         (`A member serving on the committee` OF `the Minister of Justice`, d),
         (`A member serving on the committee` OF `another minister whom the Government names`, e),
         (`A member serving on the committee` OF `the Knesset member of the coalition factions`, f),
         (`A member serving on the committee` OF `the Knesset member of the opposition factions`, g),
         (`A member serving on the committee` OF `the public representative whom the coalition Knesset members chose`, h),
         (`A member serving on the committee` OF `the public representative whom the opposition Knesset members chose`, i)

`no day is relevant` MEANS
    `The days relevant to section 4B` OF NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING

-- Elections on 3 November 2026 (hypothetical): the 90th day before is 5 August 2026 (31 + 30 + 29 days back from 3 November to 5 August is 90).
`elections on 3 November 2026, members chosen on 20 November 2026` MEANS
    `The days relevant to section 4B` OF (JUST (Date 3 11 2026)), NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, (JUST (Date 20 11 2026))

`elections on 3 November 2026, members not yet chosen` MEANS
    `The days relevant to section 4B` OF (JUST (Date 3 11 2026)), NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING

`a ground for elections arose on 1 January 2027` MEANS
    `The days relevant to section 4B` OF NOTHING, (JUST (Date 1 1 2027)), NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING

`the Government resigned on 10 March 2027` MEANS
    `The days relevant to section 4B` OF NOTHING, NOTHING, (JUST (Date 10 3 2027)), NOTHING, NOTHING

`no confidence was expressed on 15 April 2027` MEANS
    `The days relevant to section 4B` OF NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, (JUST (Date 15 4 2027)), NOTHING

§ `s 4(c): may the committee act, is there a quorum`

#ASSERT `the committee may act with this many members` 9 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the committee may act with this many members` 7 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the committee may act with this many members` 6 EQUALS FALSE
-- The quorum of five is in the instrument (SH 3388 p. 434, s 1(2)) and not in the consolidation.
#ASSERT `a meeting of the committee has a quorum` 5 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `a meeting of the committee has a quorum` 4 EQUALS FALSE

§ `Which vintage applies on a day (Amendment No. 4 s 3)`

-- The 26th Knesset's term begins 1 December 2026 (hypothetical); a committee is set up under the new text on 15 December 2026 (hypothetical).
#ASSERT `the vintage that applies on` (Date 30 11 2026) (JUST (Date 1 12 2026)) (JUST (Date 15 12 2026)) EQUALS `the text before the 26th Knesset`
#ASSERT `the vintage that applies on` (Date 1 12 2026) (JUST (Date 1 12 2026)) (JUST (Date 15 12 2026)) EQUALS `the transitional window of Amendment No. 4 section 3`
#ASSERT `the vintage that applies on` (Date 14 12 2026) (JUST (Date 1 12 2026)) (JUST (Date 15 12 2026)) EQUALS `the transitional window of Amendment No. 4 section 3`
#ASSERT `the vintage that applies on` (Date 15 12 2026) (JUST (Date 1 12 2026)) (JUST (Date 15 12 2026)) EQUALS `the text from the 26th Knesset`
-- No committee set up under the new text yet: the transitional rule still applies.
#ASSERT `the vintage that applies on` (Date 1 1 2030) (JUST (Date 1 12 2026)) NOTHING EQUALS `the transitional window of Amendment No. 4 section 3`
-- The term has not begun: the text before.
#ASSERT `the vintage that applies on` (Date 1 1 2030) NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS `the text before the 26th Knesset`

#ASSERT `the committee may elect judges in this vintage` `the text before the 26th Knesset` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the committee may elect judges in this vintage` `the transitional window of Amendment No. 4 section 3` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the committee may elect judges in this vintage` `the text from the 26th Knesset` EQUALS TRUE

§ `s 4B: the periods when the committee may not elect judges`

-- Elections on 3 November 2026; the 90th day before is 5 August 2026.
#ASSERT `section 4B bars the election of judges on` `elections on 3 November 2026, members not yet chosen` (Date 4 8 2026) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `section 4B bars the election of judges on` `elections on 3 November 2026, members not yet chosen` (Date 5 8 2026) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `section 4B bars the election of judges on` `elections on 3 November 2026, members not yet chosen` (Date 3 11 2026) EQUALS TRUE
-- Members chosen on 20 November: barred on the 19th; on the 20th the bar no longer applies (fork E1: it runs to the day before they are chosen).
#ASSERT `section 4B bars the election of judges on` `elections on 3 November 2026, members chosen on 20 November 2026` (Date 19 11 2026) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `section 4B bars the election of judges on` `elections on 3 November 2026, members chosen on 20 November 2026` (Date 20 11 2026) EQUALS FALSE
-- A ground for elections from the day it arises.
#ASSERT `section 4B bars the election of judges on` `a ground for elections arose on 1 January 2027` (Date 31 12 2026) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `section 4B bars the election of judges on` `a ground for elections arose on 1 January 2027` (Date 1 1 2027) EQUALS TRUE
-- The Government's resignation, and a vote of no confidence.
#ASSERT `section 4B bars the election of judges on` `the Government resigned on 10 March 2027` (Date 9 3 2027) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `section 4B bars the election of judges on` `the Government resigned on 10 March 2027` (Date 10 3 2027) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `section 4B bars the election of judges on` `no confidence was expressed on 15 April 2027` (Date 15 4 2027) EQUALS TRUE
-- Nothing relevant: no bar.
#ASSERT `section 4B bars the election of judges on` `no day is relevant` (Date 1 1 2028) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `ninety days before` (JUST (Date 3 11 2026)) EQUALS JUST (Date 5 8 2026)
-- Other decisions in a barred period: all the members serving.
#ASSERT `all the members serving consent` (`the nine from the 26th Knesset in order` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `all the members serving consent` (`the nine from the 26th Knesset in order` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE

§ `s 4A: the Minister's decision on a deadlock, and the month rule`

-- The first term ended on 10 March 2027 (the later day); the Knesset began on 1 December 2026: a year from 10 March 2027 is 10 March 2028.
#ASSERT `the Minister of Justice may decide that section 4A applies` (`A calendar day` OF 10, 3, 2027) (`A calendar day` OF 1, 12, 2026) (JUST (`A calendar day` OF 10, 3, 2028)) FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the Minister of Justice may decide that section 4A applies` (`A calendar day` OF 10, 3, 2027) (`A calendar day` OF 1, 12, 2026) (JUST (`A calendar day` OF 9, 3, 2028)) FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- The new Knesset's term is the later day: first term ended 1 June 2026, Knesset began 1 December 2026: a year from 1 December 2026 is 1 December 2027.
#ASSERT `the Minister of Justice may decide that section 4A applies` (`A calendar day` OF 1, 6, 2026) (`A calendar day` OF 1, 12, 2026) (JUST (`A calendar day` OF 1, 12, 2027)) FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the Minister of Justice may decide that section 4A applies` (`A calendar day` OF 1, 6, 2026) (`A calendar day` OF 1, 12, 2026) (JUST (`A calendar day` OF 30, 11, 2027)) FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Once only in the term of that Knesset (s 4A(a)(2)).
#ASSERT `the Minister of Justice may decide that section 4A applies` (`A calendar day` OF 10, 3, 2027) (`A calendar day` OF 1, 12, 2026) (JUST (`A calendar day` OF 10, 3, 2028)) TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- No vote in which no judge was elected: no power.
#ASSERT `the Minister of Justice may decide that section 4A applies` (`A calendar day` OF 10, 3, 2027) (`A calendar day` OF 1, 12, 2026) NOTHING FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- The month rule, s 4A(d)(1): proposed 15 March 2028, a month on 15 April 2028.
#ASSERT `the proposers may choose from their own candidates` (`A calendar day` OF 15, 3, 2028) (`A calendar day` OF 14, 4, 2028) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the proposers may choose from their own candidates` (`A calendar day` OF 15, 3, 2028) (`A calendar day` OF 15, 4, 2028) EQUALS TRUE
-- December carries into January of the next year.
#ASSERT `the proposers may choose from their own candidates` (`A calendar day` OF 20, 12, 2027) (`A calendar day` OF 19, 1, 2028) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the proposers may choose from their own candidates` (`A calendar day` OF 20, 12, 2027) (`A calendar day` OF 20, 1, 2028) EQUALS TRUE

§ `s 7(4): ending a judge's term by decision of the committee`

-- Seven members in favour, proposed by the chair: valid in either vintage.
#ASSERT `the committee's decision ends the judge's term` `the Minister of Justice, as chair of the committee` (`the nine from the 26th Knesset in order` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `the text before the 26th Knesset` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the committee's decision ends the judge's term` `the Minister of Justice, as chair of the committee` (`the nine from the 26th Knesset in order` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `the text from the 26th Knesset` EQUALS TRUE
-- Six: not enough.
#ASSERT `the committee's decision ends the judge's term` `the Commissioner for Complaints against Judges` (`the nine from the 26th Knesset in order` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `the text from the 26th Knesset` EQUALS FALSE
-- The President of the Supreme Court may propose; a stranger may not.
#ASSERT `the committee's decision ends the judge's term` `the President of the Supreme Court` (`the nine from the 26th Knesset in order` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) `the text from the 26th Knesset` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the committee's decision ends the judge's term` `someone else` (`the nine from the 26th Knesset in order` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) `the text from the 26th Knesset` EQUALS FALSE
-- In the transitional window other decisions need all the members serving (Amendment No. 4 s 3): seven of nine is not enough, nine is.
#ASSERT `the committee's decision ends the judge's term` `the Minister of Justice, as chair of the committee` (`the nine from the 26th Knesset in order` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `the transitional window of Amendment No. 4 section 3` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the committee's decision ends the judge's term` `the Minister of Justice, as chair of the committee` (`the nine from the 26th Knesset in order` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) `the transitional window of Amendment No. 4 section 3` EQUALS TRUE

§ `s 5: citizenship`

#ASSERT `the person may be appointed a judge, as to citizenship` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the person may be appointed a judge, as to citizenship` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
